## Track 2 — Accuracy Dashboard
Track and surface win rates broken down by sector, confidence tier, and source quality. This becomes our credibility layer — if our 80%+ confidence signals are actually right 80% of the time, that's the main thing we put on the landing page. No accuracy data = no trust.

> **Dependency: Track 1.3 must have at least 2 weeks of performance data before Track 2 is meaningful**

### Subtasks

**2.1 — Accuracy aggregation queries**
- Write PostgreSQL queries that aggregate `signal_performance` data by:
  - Overall win rate
  - Win rate by sector (use existing sector/geography field from signal)
  - Win rate by confidence tier (40-60 / 60-75 / 75-90 / 90+)
  - Win rate by source quality (map source domain to tier as discussed)
  - Win rate by time horizon (intraday / short-term / medium-term)
- Expose via a new REST endpoint `GET /api/accuracy`
- Cache result for 1 hour — no need to recalculate on every request

**2.2 — Accuracy dashboard page**
- Add a new `/accuracy` route to the web app
- Show overall win rate prominently at the top — big number, impossible to miss
- Break down below by sector, confidence tier, source quality
- Use simple bar charts — no fancy libraries needed, CSS bars are fine
- Show sample size next to each stat so users know if it's statistically meaningful
- Add a disclaimer: `"Past signal accuracy does not guarantee future performance"`

**2.3 — Surface accuracy on landing/login page**
- Once win rate data exists, add a single stat to the login page left panel
- Example: `"83% signal accuracy across 1,200 signals"`
- Only show if sample size > 50 signals — hide until then

